 "conclusions": [
  "Blending every candidate (all) lowers hit@5 0.912 -> 0.877 and MRR@10 0.790 -> 0.753: without the window, records with a high cosine and nothing else in their favour outrank the answers.",
  "Removing the blend (vecsignal) drops hit@5 to 0.544: the windowed blend is the strongest ranking step on this corpus.",
  "A fixed pool of 40 costs top-10 recall one question (hit@10 0.947 -> 0.930); 80 matches dev at k=10.",
  "relgate-r with pool 80 matches dev on hit@1/hit@5/MRR and recovers one question at top 10 (hit@10 and recall_all@10 0.930 -> 0.947, 0.912 -> 0.930); hook hit unchanged.",
  "Scoring short records from their stored vector (-fast) lowers hit@1 0.684 -> 0.649: stored vectors of code proxies and file summaries embed other text than searchable_text."
 ]
